{"n":5,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0012.05.01","approved-by":"build-stage (R2)","trial":"docs/trial/kernel-trial-4.md blob a5d253d5e12722956afea38e79cb7fc1cf492c7b; face blob 9aaed75fc8f0594a1289fa83e870a474d4d021d2","body":"## What We Learned\ntype: note\nby: prima-packs\nmade: 2026-11-11\nsources: docs/trial/kernel-trial.md finding 10; docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md verdicts 0012.03.14, 0012.03.16, 1001.01; DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md R9, R16; kernel/MAP.md Bob test\ndesign: DECISIONS-INDEX D64, D68, D69; docs/design/DESIGN.md section 8 Finding (:192); 00.00.00.0055 (brands law)\n\nWhat building and trialing 10.11.21.0012 (dictionary) taught us. R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88): \"the seated 05 for each page should explain what you learned\". Every line names its source; nothing here is new law.\n\n- The dictionary sections are counters 03.14 (b) and 03.16 (c) with no 03.00 and no 03.99 (R9, DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:37-38). R16 calls 03.00 a door, held `7` (QUESTIONS Q29).\n- Before R9 these counters had no board and would have failed format.md:123 \"board before counters\" (docs/trial/kernel-trial.md finding 10).\n- The index points to the brand cards in the right sections (decisions.md:458-459), as TRIAL-K2 checked for 10.11.21.1001.01 (docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md verdict).\n- Whether a counted dictionary section can be seated, and which faces are counted on which page types, are open (QUESTIONS Q22, Q35; verdicts 0012.03.14 and .16 HELD-7).\n- TRIAL-K3 (docs/trial/kernel-trial-3.md) held 0012.00: pointer registry fields are not written (Q33), faces: form (Q39), counted faces per page type (Q22).","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0012"}
{"n":6,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0012.05.02","approved-by":"build-stage (R2)","trial":"docs/trial/kernel-trial-5.md blob 86eb3a58e028d9b23e0a94cd4577329195300f99; face blob dd89a5199d1a0b47f5cac3bce2ec0e8185ff1ce6","body":"## Pack Header\nby: prima-packs\nauthorized: 7 (no approved N4 revision exists for this page; the pack is asked for by R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88); QUESTIONS Q45)\nlead: 7 (no band default is seated, workflow-loop.003.md:107)\naxioms: 5.3.9\noutcome: the sample dictionary indexes every word the samples use, 03.00 is decided, its sections are reviewed, and the compute resolves `bob` and `cats` from the real books\noverview: the sample book's dictionary: page 0012, face 03, an index from each word to its brand cards\nstop if: a step needs the answer to an open question (listed in blocked-by); save the question in kernel/QUESTIONS.md and move on (R22 \"save questions\"); never seat your own work (R2, R20)\ngrant: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.0012.*.draft.md (not face 00 or 05); books/10.11.21.book via node kernel/build.mjs\nframe: 7 (no approved MVP frame ID, workflow-loop.003.md:113)\nrisk: 7 (sample fixture, not kernel law)\npredecessor: 8c8f780 (kernel pass 3), fae009a (kernel pass 4)\ndesign: DECISIONS-INDEX D64, D68, D69; docs/design/DESIGN.md section 8 Finding (:192); 00.00.00.0055 (brands law)\nlinks: 00.00.00.0055 (brands law), 10.11.21.1001 (bob brand cards), 10.11.21.0013 (common questions)\nopen: Q22, Q29, Q35, Q41\n\nThe MVP pack for 10.11.21.0012 (dictionary): the agents.md-style build list (workflow-loop.003.md:99) to bring this page to its MVP. Steps are work cards w01 onward (workflow-loop.003.md:122). Each says what it depends on, what blocks it (question ids in kernel/QUESTIONS.md, Qnn, or docs/design/OPEN.md, Onn), and the test that shows it is done.\n\n## w01\ntype: work\ntitle: settle 03.00 and how dictionary sections are reviewed\nreason: R16 vs R9; seqAddr.md:199 \"A counted face is never seated\"\ndepends: none\nblocked-by: Q22, Q29, Q35\ndone: Q22, Q29 and Q35 in kernel/QUESTIONS.md each have a recorded answer; the files and the faces: line on 10.11.21.0012.00 match it (a 03.00 file exists only if Q22/Q29 rule it; each 03.NN section is draft or seated as Q35 rules); and node kernel/build.mjs --check exits 0\npath: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.0012.*\nask: >build settle 03.00 and how dictionary sections are reviewed\n\n## w02\ntype: work\ntitle: prove the compute resolves bob and cats from the real books\nreason: Bob test session 1 (kernel/MAP.md Bob test)\ndepends: none\nblocked-by: none\ndone: a crates/compute test on the real books asks /brands for `bob` and `cats` and gets 10.11.21.1001.01.bob and .cats\npath: crates/compute/tests/\nask: >build prove the compute resolves bob and cats from the real books\n\n## w03\ntype: work\ntitle: index every word the samples use\nreason: the outcome asks for a dictionary that indexes every word the samples use; today it has bob (03.14) and cats (03.16) only\ndepends: w01\nblocked-by: none\ndone: every brand card key on the sample pages (10.11.21.*.01 cards with type: brand) has a 03.NN section on 10.11.21.0012 that points to it, checked by a script or test that lists brand keys and dictionary words and finds none missing; node kernel/build.mjs --check exits 0\npath: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.0012.03.*.draft.md\nask: >build index every word the samples use\n\n## w04\ntype: work\ntitle: fresh-session hostile trial of the 10.11.21.0012.03 sections\nreason: a face needs a hostile trial from a different view before an R2 seat (axiom 9; R2, R20)\ndepends: w01, w03 (both may change the sections)\nblocked-by: none\ndone: a docs/trial/ file by a session that did not build the faces (R20, DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:78-80) gives each 10.11.21.0012.03.NN section PASS, FAIL or HELD-7 with its full git blob\npath: docs/trial/\nask: >build Trial the 10.11.21.0012.03 sections as a fresh session; report only.\n\n## w05\ntype: work\ntitle: seat the passing sections under R2\nreason: R2, R20; the outcome asks for the sections to be reviewed\ndepends: w04\nblocked-by: Q35 (only a face 05 counter may be seated until a ruling allows other counters; kernel/build.mjs refuses others), Q34\ndone: seat-03.NN lines with the trial and full blob in 10.11.21.0012.00, and node kernel/build.mjs --check exits 0\npath: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.0012.00.draft.md\nask: >build seat the passing dictionary sections under R2","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0012"}
{"n":7,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.00.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.","body":"---\naddress: 10.11.21.0013\ntitle: common-questions\ntype: general\nstate: draft\nwhy-draft: sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.\n---\n\n## Registry\nfaces: 01 draft, 04 draft, 05.01 seated, 05.02 draft\nseat-05.01: approved-by: build-stage (R2); trial: docs/trial/kernel-trial-5.md blob 86eb3a58e028d9b23e0a94cd4577329195300f99; blob: 16146a0fa073fc947138de43033f9e9a2b75ac09\nwhy-01: sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it. The `question` card type is not in the kernel card-type table (decisions.md C8.9); `7`.\nwhy-04: sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.\nwhy-05.02: R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88) MVP work pack for this page, written by lane PACKS; not trialed or linted yet (workflow-loop.003.md:171, axiom 9); `authorized` and `frame` are `7` (QUESTIONS Q45). Seating is QUESTIONS Q41.\n\nR10 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:40), R12 (:53) and R19 (:75): face 00 holds the stamp, the page type and the registry. Layout follows docs/spec/face00.md (DRAFT, not ruled): `why-draft` and `why-NN` are PROPOSED names there; `seat-NN` is the build's own (`7`, QUESTIONS Q34); per-type registry fields are not written (`7`, Q33); `faces:` is written here and checked by the builder against the files (written vs derived is `7`, face00.md F2, CONFLICTS D5).\n\nR11 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:44): the common questions list. Page number `0013` is `7`: chosen in 0010-0019 (static, R17) to match crates/ask (COMPUTE); the Director has not placed it.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":8,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.01.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it. The `question` card type is not in the kernel card-type table (decisions.md C8.9); `7`.","body":"## what is my name\ntype: question\nforms: what is my name\nanswer: 10.11.21.1001.01.bob\n\nR11 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:44): \"The what is my name will become part of a common questions people ask list. When we see a version of this, it becomes linked as a sentence; it works like brands do.\" `7`: the card fields (`type: question`, `forms`, `answer`) match crates/ask `QuestionCard`; the Director has not given them.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":9,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.04.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.","body":"## what is my name\nsource: [01 / what is my name] Bob test, session 2 question; why: docs/spec/DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:44\nwhy: This is how we let the compute solve.\n\nWhen the user asks \"what is my name\", the key words what + my + name match this question, and it points to the bob card, the user's name.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":10,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.05.01","approved-by":"build-stage (R2)","trial":"docs/trial/kernel-trial-5.md blob 86eb3a58e028d9b23e0a94cd4577329195300f99; face blob 16146a0fa073fc947138de43033f9e9a2b75ac09","body":"## What We Learned\ntype: note\nby: prima-packs\nmade: 2026-11-11\nsources: DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md R11 (:43-50); docs/BUILD-LOG.md [KERNEL] third pass, [COMPUTE] R11 ask solver, [APP] round 3; docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md verdicts 0013.00, .01, .04; kernel/CONFLICTS.md D14; kernel/MAP.md hole 15\ndesign: docs/design/DESIGN.md section 7 The compute and its queue (:168); DECISIONS-INDEX D89; DECISIONS-LOG D147, D267, D271, D290; R11\n\nWhat building and trialing 10.11.21.0013 (common-questions) taught us. R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88): \"the seated 05 for each page should explain what you learned\". Every line names its source; nothing here is new law.\n\n- R11 gave the Bob test its route: a question card `what-is-my-name` with `answer: 10.11.21.1001.01.bob`, matched by key words like brands (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:43-50; added in 8c8f780).\n- The compute side is all `7`: crates/ask scores by weighted Dice, threshold 0.5, at most 3 pieces, and probes below the threshold; the seed phrasings are \"whats my name\", \"who am i\", \"what do you call me\", \"my name?\" (docs/BUILD-LOG.md [COMPUTE] R11 lines).\n- The page number 0013 and the card fields (`type: question`, `forms`, `answer`) are the build's, copied from crates/ask QuestionCard, not the Director's (kernel/MAP.md hole 15; CONFLICTS D14; QUESTIONS Q49). TRIAL-K2 held all three faces on this (verdicts 0013.00, .01, .04).\n- The app's Ask screen reads the common-questions page as READER_BOOK.0013, also `7` (docs/BUILD-LOG.md [APP] round 3).\n- TRIAL-K3 (docs/trial/kernel-trial-3.md) held 0013.00: page number 0013 is `7` (R11) and the page type for common questions is open (face00.md F10, Q33).","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":11,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.05.02.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88) MVP work pack for this page, written by lane PACKS; not trialed or linted yet (workflow-loop.003.md:171, axiom 9); `authorized` and `frame` are `7` (QUESTIONS Q45). Seating is QUESTIONS Q41.","body":"## Pack Header\nby: prima-packs\nauthorized: 7 (no approved N4 revision exists for this page; the pack is asked for by R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88); QUESTIONS Q45)\nlead: 7 (no band default is seated, workflow-loop.003.md:107)\naxioms: 5.3.9\noutcome: the common-questions page has a ruled number and card fields, its question cards are seated, and \"what is my name\" reaches the bob card end to end from the real books through /ask and the app\noverview: R11: common questions linked like brands; the compute hands the model 1-3 pieces or probes the person\nstop if: a step needs the answer to an open question (listed in blocked-by); save the question in kernel/QUESTIONS.md and move on (R22 \"save questions\"); never seat your own work (R2, R20)\ngrant: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.0013.*.draft.md (not face 00 or 05); books/10.11.21.book via node kernel/build.mjs; crates/ask, crates/compute, app/\nframe: 7 (no approved MVP frame ID, workflow-loop.003.md:113)\nrisk: 7 (sample fixture; the ask solver is compute code)\npredecessor: 8c8f780 (kernel pass 3), the COMPUTE R11 work in docs/BUILD-LOG.md\ndesign: docs/design/DESIGN.md section 7 The compute and its queue (:168); DECISIONS-INDEX D89; DECISIONS-LOG D147, D267, D271, D290; R11\nlinks: 10.11.21.1001 (answer: bob), 10.11.21.0012 (dictionary), 00.00.00.0055 (brands law), 00.00.00.0054 (question card type)\nopen: Q33, Q49; CONFLICTS D14; O18\n\nThe MVP pack for 10.11.21.0013 (common-questions): the agents.md-style build list (workflow-loop.003.md:99) to bring this page to its MVP. Steps are work cards w01 onward (workflow-loop.003.md:122). Each says what it depends on, what blocks it (question ids in kernel/QUESTIONS.md, Qnn, or docs/design/OPEN.md, Onn), and the test that shows it is done.\n\n## w01\ntype: work\ntitle: rule the page number and the question card fields\nreason: both are the build's `7` (MAP hole 15, CONFLICTS D14)\ndepends: none\nblocked-by: Q33, Q49\ndone: the common-questions page sits at the ruled number in the kernel/samples/10.11.21 file names and books/10.11.21.book, in crates/compute/src/store.rs (the common-questions page number) and in the app (app/app/ask/page.tsx `/page/${BOOK}.0013`, app/components/AskBox.tsx); and 00.00.00.0054.02 lists the question card type with its fields, and this page's question cards use them (TRIAL-K5 finding 7)\npath: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.0013.*, kernel/00.00.00/00.00.00.0054.02.draft.md, crates/compute/src/store.rs, app/app/ask/page.tsx, app/components/AskBox.tsx\nask: >build rule the page number and the question card fields\n\n## w02\ntype: work\ntitle: test \"what is my name\" end to end on the real books\nreason: R11 is how the compute solves (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:44)\ndepends: none\nblocked-by: none\ndone: a crates/compute test on a copy of books/ posts /ask \"what is my name\" and gets 10.11.21.1001.01.bob with state seated (1001.01 is seated, blob 5415cef2dd0a37f3c2ba4c9b6d2652262f0ef82d, and the seated face wins, R5; crates/compute/src/askq.rs face_text), and a nonsense prompt gets a probe\npath: crates/compute/tests/\nask: >build test \"what is my name\" end to end on the real books\n\n## w03\ntype: work\ntitle: check \"what is my name\" in the app's Ask screen\nreason: the outcome says end to end \"through /ask and the app\"; w02 covers /ask only (TRIAL-K5 finding 7)\ndepends: w02\nblocked-by: none\ndone: a script under app/scripts/, run against the compute serving a copy of books/, opens the Ask screen, asks \"what is my name\", and exits 0 only if the answer shows bob from 10.11.21.1001.01 (and exits non-zero otherwise); the common-questions list on the screen is read from the ruled page number\npath: app/scripts/\nask: >build check \"what is my name\" in the app's Ask screen\n\n## w04\ntype: work\ntitle: fresh-session hostile trial of 10.11.21.0013.01, .04\nreason: a face needs a hostile trial from a different view before an R2 seat (axiom 9; R2, R20)\ndepends: w01 (it changes the card fields on 0013.01 and .04)\nblocked-by: none\ndone: a docs/trial/ file by a session that did not build the faces (R20, DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:78-80) gives each of 10.11.21.0013.01, .04 PASS, FAIL or HELD-7 with its git blob\npath: docs/trial/\nask: >build Trial 10.11.21.0013.01, .04 as a fresh session; report only.\n\n## w05\ntype: work\ntitle: seat the passing faces under R2\nreason: R2, R20, R22\ndepends: the trial step\nblocked-by: Q34\ndone: seat-NN lines in 10.11.21.0013.00 and node kernel/build.mjs --check exits 0\npath: kernel/samples/10.11.21/\nask: >build seat the passing faces under R2","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":12,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.00.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.","body":"---\naddress: 10.11.21.1001\ntitle: bob\ntype: general\nstate: draft\nwhy-draft: sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.\n---\n\n## Registry\nfaces: 01 seated, 05.01 seated, 05.02 seated\nseat-01: approved-by: build-stage (R2); trial: docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md blob da5d51424fee3bea1d8443c619fcba3c534a1ace; blob: 5415cef2dd0a37f3c2ba4c9b6d2652262f0ef82d\nseat-05.01: approved-by: build-stage (R2); trial: docs/trial/kernel-trial-4.md blob a5d253d5e12722956afea38e79cb7fc1cf492c7b; blob: 566071064f63a5c85fcb3bd87d9e375717bdbf51\nseat-05.02: approved-by: build-stage (R2); trial: docs/trial/kernel-trial-4.md blob a5d253d5e12722956afea38e79cb7fc1cf492c7b; blob: 2aa3490239620604ce1bb13c34841a60ac8f7056\n\nR10 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:40), R12 (:53) and R19 (:75): face 00 holds the stamp, the page type and the registry. Layout follows docs/spec/face00.md (DRAFT, not ruled): `why-draft` and `why-NN` are PROPOSED names there; `seat-NN` is the build's own (`7`, QUESTIONS Q34); per-type registry fields are not written (`7`, Q33); `faces:` is written here and checked by the builder against the files (written vs derived is `7`, face00.md F2, CONFLICTS D5).\n\nR15 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:62): a brand card on face 01 needs no 04 card, so the `04` face that held the bob and cats whys was removed in kernel pass 3.\n\nR2 seat (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:7-9, R20 :78-80): face 01 passed TRIAL-K2 and is seated at the cited blob; this face 00 stays a draft (R14). Where a seat record lives is `7` (QUESTIONS Q34): it is kept here, in `seat-01:`, so the seated face itself is unchanged.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
{"n":13,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.01","approved-by":"build-stage (R2)","trial":"docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md blob da5d51424fee3bea1d8443c619fcba3c534a1ace; face blob 5415cef2dd0a37f3c2ba4c9b6d2652262f0ef82d","body":"## bob\ntype: brand\nbrand: bob.001\nforms: Bob\nmeans: the user's name\n\n## cats\ntype: brand\nbrand: cats.001\nforms: cats\nmeans: animals the user likes","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
{"n":14,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.05.01","approved-by":"build-stage (R2)","trial":"docs/trial/kernel-trial-4.md blob a5d253d5e12722956afea38e79cb7fc1cf492c7b; face blob 566071064f63a5c85fcb3bd87d9e375717bdbf51","body":"## What We Learned\ntype: note\nby: prima-packs\nmade: 2026-11-11\nsources: commit 42ffbc9; docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md verdict 1001.01 PASS and finding 20; DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md R15; docs/BUILD-LOG.md [APP] round 3\ndesign: DECISIONS-INDEX D65-D67 (brands), D02 (R2 seats); docs/design/DESIGN.md section 8 Finding (:192)\n\nWhat building and trialing 10.11.21.1001 (bob) taught us. R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88): \"the seated 05 for each page should explain what you learned\". Every line names its source; nothing here is new law.\n\n- Face 01 (brand cards bob and cats) passed TRIAL-K2 and was seated at blob 5415cef2 under R2 and R20 (commit 42ffbc9), while face 00 stays a draft (R14).\n- R15 removed the bob and cats 04 face; a compute test still expected it and failed (docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md finding 20; crates/compute/tests/http.rs:261), routed to COMPUTE.\n- The seqpage check disagrees with the kernel face 00: check.seq on the exported page flags \"stamp state draft disagrees with the page's entries (live)\" and \"seat-01: is not a registry field for type general\" (docs/BUILD-LOG.md [APP] round 3). That is QUESTIONS Q31, Q34 and Q38 showing up in a real page.\n- TRIAL-K3 (docs/trial/kernel-trial-3.md, finding 14) reports the same stamp-state clash from the trial side and raised it as Q40.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
{"n":15,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.05.02","approved-by":"build-stage (R2)","trial":"docs/trial/kernel-trial-4.md blob a5d253d5e12722956afea38e79cb7fc1cf492c7b; face blob 2aa3490239620604ce1bb13c34841a60ac8f7056","body":"## Pack Header\nby: prima-packs\nauthorized: 7 (no approved N4 revision exists for this page; the pack is asked for by R22 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:86-88); QUESTIONS Q45)\nlead: 7 (no band default is seated, workflow-loop.003.md:107)\naxioms: 5.3.9\noutcome: 10.11.21.1001 keeps face 01 seated and unchanged, its face 00 passes both the builder and the seqpage check, and both Bob test sessions pass on the real books\noverview: the Bob test fixture: the user's name and what they like, as brand cards\nstop if: a step needs the answer to an open question (listed in blocked-by); save the question in kernel/QUESTIONS.md and move on (R22 \"save questions\"); never seat your own work (R2, R20)\ngrant: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.1001.00.draft.md (only after Q31, Q34, Q38 are ruled); face 01 is seated and not touched\nframe: 7 (no approved MVP frame ID, workflow-loop.003.md:113)\nrisk: 7 (sample fixture)\npredecessor: 42ffbc9 (seat of 1001.01)\ndesign: DECISIONS-INDEX D65-D67 (brands), D02 (R2 seats); docs/design/DESIGN.md section 8 Finding (:192)\nlinks: 10.11.21.0012 (dictionary index to bob, cats), 10.11.21.0013 (what is my name -> bob), 00.00.00.0055 (brands law)\nopen: Q31, Q34, Q38\n\nThe MVP pack for 10.11.21.1001 (bob): the agents.md-style build list (workflow-loop.003.md:99) to bring this page to its MVP. Steps are work cards w01 onward (workflow-loop.003.md:122). Each says what it depends on, what blocks it (question ids in kernel/QUESTIONS.md, Qnn, or docs/design/OPEN.md, Onn), and the test that shows it is done.\n\n## w01\ntype: work\ntitle: keep 1001.01 exactly as trialed\nreason: R2 seat at blob 5415cef2; any change needs a new trial (axiom 9)\ndepends: none\nblocked-by: none\ndone: node kernel/build.mjs --check exits 0 and git hash-object kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.1001.01.md starts with 5415cef2\npath: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.1001.01.md\nask: >build Check 1001.01 is unchanged; do not edit it.\n\n## w02\ntype: work\ntitle: make the builder and the seqpage check agree on this face 00\nreason: check.seq findings on this page (docs/BUILD-LOG.md [APP] round 3)\ndepends: none\nblocked-by: Q31, Q34, Q38\ndone: POST /check.seq on the exported 10.11.21.1001 returns no stamp-state or seat-01 finding\npath: kernel/samples/10.11.21/10.11.21.1001.00.draft.md, crates/seqpage/src/face00.rs\nask: >build make the builder and the seqpage check agree on this face 00\n\n## w03\ntype: work\ntitle: run both Bob test sessions on the real books\nreason: session 1 types bob; session 2 asks what is my name (kernel/MAP.md Bob test)\ndepends: 10.11.21.0012 and 10.11.21.0013 packs\nblocked-by: none\ndone: compute tests on a copy of books/ pass for /brands bob and /ask \"what is my name\"\npath: crates/compute/tests/\nask: >build run both Bob test sessions on the real books","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
